Z||000002||Black88GT||06-21-2001||01:36 PM||||Check out <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mrmikes.com</A>  for nice leather seats.  You recover them yourself, from what I have heard its really easy, he gives you a tape and all the supplies/tools you need.<P>I think the Fiero store sells clothe replacements but there not too much less then the leather seats. ||||reg||14
Z||000003||stimpy||06-21-2001||01:43 PM||||I think if I'm reading right, Dealer has seen the upholstury kits, but would rather just go with newer seats. In that case, keep checking the mall section. FieroDave usually has a good selection of take out seats from low mile cars. Other reliable sources would be Pondski and 007Doug. (Not to slight anyone I haven't mentioned, but these guys have been around a while and have established impeccable reputations.) ||||reg||1
